# LCN docs via CLI

When creating, editing, publishing, organizing, or laying out LCN site docs/collections/home slots, use the terminal CLI — do **not** open `index/editor.html` or drive the browser UI.

## How to run

From the repo root:

```bash
node scripts/lcn-docs/cli.js <command> ...
```

Requires one-time setup: `scripts/lcn-docs/serviceAccount.json` + `npm install` in `scripts/lcn-docs` (see `scripts/lcn-docs/README.md`).

## Common commands

- `list` / `get <id>` — inspect docs (`--json` when parsing)
- `create` / `update <id>` / `set-content <id> <file>` — write meta + body (HTML or light Markdown)
- `publish` / `unpublish` / `delete`
- `list-on <id> --projects|--development|--updates` (and `--off-*`)
- `collection list|create|add-page|add-section|move|dissolve`
- `home get` / `home set --featured ... --side ... --recent ...`

## Content notes

- Body HTML matches what the contenteditable editor stores.
- Images live under `a_home_assets/`; prefer paths like `a_home_assets/content/...` or full URLs in `images` / `<img src>`.
- Public URL shape: `index/doc.html?v=<docId>`.

Do not use the in-page OpenAI “Ask AI” flow for bulk site edits; use this CLI from Cursor.
